cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Cyberdeception Atlas dataset, evidence model, or evaluation
  protocol, please cite this release.
title: 'Cyberdeception Atlas: Source-Bounded Corpus and Evidence Architecture'
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Pacheco
    given-names: Federico
version: '2026.10'
date-released: 2026-10-02
url: 'https://cyberdeceptionatlas.org'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/fedequark/cyberdeception-atlas'
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - cyber deception
  - defensive deception
  - honeypot
  - honeytoken
  - evidence synthesis
  - cybersecurity evaluation
abstract: >-
  A bilingual, source-linked corpus and reference implementation for mapping
  defensive cyber-deception techniques, environments, evidence types, and
  review depth. Release candidate 2026.10 contains 190 public records, 24
  single-reviewer full-text syntheses, 50 source-bounded critical readings,
  reproducible corpus analyses, and an isolated conformance test of the
  reporting schema.
